WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
Hi, you found this intro easter egg.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.080
I'm Nilson, senior product designer
living in Lisbon, South Bay.

3
00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:13.500
I've been designing for 14 years
and the last 8 focused on technical products.

4
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:19.280
Some of the companies I have contributed to
in recent years are Grafana Labs in observability

5
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.040
and Dynatrace in platform governance.

6
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.380
Three things define my work.

7
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.240
I design the invisible before anything else.

8
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:32.320
So before a screen or a word exists,
I work the problem space,

9
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.400
user flows and information architecture

10
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:40.320
and the mental model the whole team needs
to talk about the problem.

11
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:46.600
At Grafana, besides redesigning the onboarding
experience that is still in place today,

12
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.600
I also designed two greenfield products
in observability

13
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:56.400
and took them to launch
against Datadog and New Relic,

14
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:03.000
building working prototypes instead of
static mockups before the age of AI.

15
00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:08.820
As a design engineer, I realized AI has
changed who a design system is for.

16
00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:14.160
So I built a design system that serves
both engineers and AI agents.

17
00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.920
So what do you get from me?

18
00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.060
You get someone who thinks in systems
and designs from understanding.

19
00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:25.840
Who prototypes until the answer is testable.

20
00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.500
And who doesn't wait for a brief.

21
00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:34.040
Because the best work I've done started
before anyone wrote one down.

22
00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.500
Let's chat.
